Package: addivortesr
Title: Bayesian Additive Voronoi Tessellation Regression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Leo", "Thomson", , "leo@feasibly.co.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bindings to the 'addivortes' Rust crate, an implementation of
    the AddiVortes method of Stone and Gosling (2025)
    <doi:10.1080/10618600.2024.2414104>: Bayesian regression on a sum of
    Voronoi tessellations, sampled by a Gibbs backfitting sampler with
    structural Metropolis-Hastings moves. Provides fitting with Gaussian,
    robust Student-t, and binary probit response families, posterior-mean
    and per-draw prediction, posterior-predictive and credible intervals,
    pointwise log-likelihood for 'loo', draws export for 'posterior', and
    'parsnip' engine registration. Note this package is NOT the original
    authors' 'AddiVortes' R implementation; it wraps the 'addivortes' Rust
    crate. The package name is provisional pre-release.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/l-thomson/addivortes
BugReports: https://github.com/l-thomson/addivortes/issues
